Introduction
   This licence agreement (the "Agreement") governs the use of the mailmcp
   software in any form, including its documentation and updates (the
   "Software"). The Software is a copyrighted work whose economic rights are
   exercised by the Licensor. THIS IS NOT OPEN SOURCE. By installing or
   using the Software the Licensee accepts this Agreement.

1. Definitions
   a) "Licensee" means the natural or legal person who installs or uses the
      Software or who has acquired a licence to a paid Tier.
   b) "User" means a natural person who actually uses the Software, in
      particular through a user token or a configuration.
   c) "Tier" means the scope of the licence under Article 2 (Free,
      Personal, Unlimited).
   d) "Licence Key" means a key issued by the Licensor that determines the
      Tier of a paid licence.
   e) "Running Installation" means one separately operated instance of the
      Software able to serve Users or mailboxes (for example one server, one
      deployment on a hosting platform or one installation in the Claude
      Desktop application). Several processes or replicas of the same
      deployment sharing one configuration form one Running Installation. A
      temporary instance created solely for an upgrade, a backup or disaster
      recovery is not another Running Installation unless it is used for
      regular operation at the same time.
   f) "Consumer" means a Licensee who is a natural person acting outside the
      scope of their business or independent profession (Section 419 of the
      Czech Civil Code).
   g) "Hosted Service" means the mailmcp.ai service operated by the
      Licensor.
   h) "Technical Protection Measures" means technical measures intended to
      protect the licence, its verification, the Tier limits, the
      integrity of the Software or access to it.

2. Grant of licence and Tiers
   2.1 The Licensor grants the Licensee a non-exclusive, non-transferable
       licence to use the Software within the Tier chosen, without the
       right to grant sublicences. A licence to a paid Tier arises upon
       payment of the licence fee; a licence to the Free Tier arises upon
       installation of the Software.
   2.2 Free: without a Licence Key and free of charge; each natural person
       may use at most 2 different mailboxes in total in the Free Tier,
       across all Running Installations (including the Hosted Service),
       configurations and user tokens; a mailbox counts once however many
       tokens contain it. A Free user token created before version 0.7.0
       keeps the limit it was created with: its User may use up to
       5 different mailboxes in total; the 2-mailbox total applies to Free
       tokens and Running Installations created from version 0.7.0 on.
       Every message the Software composes carries the "Sent with
       mailmcp.ai" signature under Article 6.
   2.3 Personal: one Running Installation whose only User is one natural
       person, with at most 5 different mailboxes in total for that User
       across all Running Installations, configurations and user tokens; a
       mailbox counts once however many tokens contain it. It does not
       matter who owns the mailboxes (the person's own mailboxes, the
       mailboxes of their business as a sole trader or the mailboxes of a
       company they work for). Other persons, in particular employees or
       assistants, may not use the Software under a Personal licence.
   2.4 Unlimited: one Running Installation in shared-server mode for an
       unlimited number of Users and mailboxes within one organization. An
       organization means one legal person, or one natural person carrying
       on business, together with its employees, the members of its
       statutory and supervisory bodies and the contractors who work on its
       behalf for its internal purposes. Commercial use inside the
       organization is permitted.
   2.5 Each additional Running Installation of a paid Tier requires an
       additional licence. A licence may be moved to another Running
       Installation at any time as long as the Licensee never operates more
       Running Installations of a paid Tier than they hold licences. The
       number of Running Installations in the Free Tier is not limited,
       but the limit of 2 mailboxes per natural person under Article 2.2
       applies in total across all of them.
   2.6 Articles 3 and 8 do not apply to the Free Tier.
   2.7 Through Stripe Managed Payments, Stripe acts as the merchant of
       record for the relevant transaction and handles payment processing,
       applicable taxes, receipts/invoices and refunds. The licence to the
       Software is granted by the Licensor.

3. Licence Key
   3.1 The paid Tiers of the Software require a Licence Key issued by the
       Licensor. The Free Tier does not require a Licence Key.
   3.2 The Licence Key is verified locally; the Software does not contact
       the Licensor to verify it.
   3.3 The Licence Key is confidential. The Licensee may not disclose it to
       third parties other than persons authorised to administer the
       Licensee's licensed Running Installations.

4. Form of delivery and interference with the Software
   4.1 The Software is delivered only as a built package (the Licensor's
       distribution repository and the MCPB package). The Licensor does not
       provide the source code of the Software and this Agreement creates
       no obligation to provide it.
   4.2 The Licensee may use and configure the built package for their
       licensed Running Installations. The Licensee's employees and
       contractors may administer the installation on the Licensee's
       behalf under the same restrictions.
   4.3 The Licensee may not decompile, reverse-engineer, modify or
       otherwise interfere with the Software beyond what Section 66 of Act
       No. 121/2000 Coll., the Czech Copyright Act, permits a lawful user.
   4.4 The Licensee may not remove, disable or circumvent the licence
       verification, the Tier limits, the Free Tier signature or the
       Technical Protection Measures, or publish modified versions of the
       Software, except where such interference cannot be prohibited under
       mandatory law (in particular Section 66 of the Czech Copyright
       Act).
   4.5 This Agreement does not affect the rights of a lawful user under
       Section 66 of Act No. 121/2000 Coll., the Czech Copyright Act, in
       particular the right to correct errors, to study and test the
       functioning of the Software and to achieve its interoperability.

5. Prohibited use
   5.1 The Licensee may not
       a) use the Software without a valid licence or beyond the Tier
          acquired;
       b) distribute, sell, rent, lend, sublicense or publish the Software
          or works derived from it.
   5.2 Without a separate written agreement with the Licensor, the Licensee
       further may not
       a) use the Software to process mailboxes of third parties as part of
          a service provided to them (for example as an agency, a managed
          IT service provider or a call centre);
       b) make the functionality of the Software available to third
          parties;
       c) operate the Software as a hosted or managed service.
   5.3 Article 5.2 does not restrict the use of the Software for the
       Licensee's own mailboxes and for the mailboxes of the persons who
       belong to the Licensee's organization under Article 2.4.

6. Copyright notices and the Free signature
   6.1 The Licensee may not remove or alter the copyright and authorship
       notices contained in the Software.
   6.2 When the Free Tier is used, every message the Software composes
       carries the "Sent with mailmcp.ai" signature; the Licensee may not
       remove or alter it. This is a separate obligation that applies to
       the Free Tier only; the signature is not required when a paid Tier
       is used.

7. Updates
   The licence includes free updates within the same major version number.
   For example, a licence purchased for version 1.x includes 1.x updates but
   need not include version 2.0. A licence purchased for version 0.x
   includes 0.x updates. An upgrade to a new major version may carry a fee;
   the Licensee may continue to use the versions the licence covers. This
   does not affect updates the Licensor is required to provide under
   mandatory law.

8. Refunds
   8.1 Within 14 days of each new purchase the Licensor refunds the full
       price of that purchase at the Licensee's request, without giving
       reasons and regardless of any statutory right of withdrawal. A new
       purchase means the first purchase of a licence, a paid upgrade to a
       new major version and the purchase of additional seats or licences.
       Requests go to info@swingingdogs.com; the refund is processed by
       Stripe as the merchant of record.
   8.2 A renewal of an existing licence or subscription is not a new
       purchase; the entitlement under Article 8.1 does not apply to it.
   8.3 A refund ends what was acquired by the purchase concerned (the
       licence, the upgrade or the additional seats); the Licensee must
       stop using the Licence Key concerned and may continue to use the
       Software only within the scope that remains or within the Free
       Tier.
   8.4 This does not affect a Consumer's statutory right to withdraw from
       the contract.

9. Warranty
   To the maximum extent permitted by law, the Software is provided "as
   is". This does not affect the Consumer's rights arising from defective
   performance or any other rights that cannot be excluded or limited by
   contract.

10. Liability
   10.1 To the extent that applicable law permits such a limitation, the
        Licensor is not liable for lost profit, lost data or indirect
        damage, and the Licensor's total liability is limited to the fees
        the Licensee paid for the licence in the most recent twelve months.
   10.2 The limitation under Article 10.1 does not apply to harm to the
        natural rights of a person or to damage caused intentionally or by
        gross negligence (Section 2898 of the Czech Civil Code), and it
        does not apply to Consumers.
   10.3 The Software operates on the Licensee's mail accounts; the Licensee
        is responsible for passwords, permissions and the content of
        messages sent.

11. Termination
   11.1 If the Licensee materially breaches this Agreement, the Licensor
        notifies the Licensee of the breach in writing or by e-mail. If the
        Licensee does not remedy the breach within 14 days of receiving the
        notice, the licence ends when that period expires.
   11.2 The Licensor may terminate the licence with immediate effect by
        written or e-mail notice if the Licensee
        a) distributes the Software without authorisation;
        b) publishes unlawfully obtained or reconstructed source code of
           the Software or a modified version of the Software;
        c) removes, disables or circumvents the licence verification or
           the Tier limits; or
        d) deliberately uses or distributes unauthorised copies of the
           Software or of Licence Keys.
   11.3 When the licence ends, the Licensee must stop using the Software
        and delete all copies of it in any form, including the built
        packages, except copies kept automatically in backups; the Licensee
        may not use such copies.
   11.4 Articles 4.3 and 4.4 (restrictions on interfering with the
        Software), Article 10 (Liability) and Article 14 (Governing law and
        disputes) survive the end of the licence.
   11.5 This does not affect the Consumer's rights that cannot be excluded
        by contract.

12. Hosted Service
   The mailmcp.ai Hosted Service is not a licence to the Software; the
   relationship is governed by the Terms of Service
   (https://mailmcp.ai/terms).

13. Consumers
   If the Licensee is a Consumer, nothing in this Agreement limits the
   rights granted to them by mandatory provisions of Czech or European
   Union law. A Consumer may turn to the Czech Trade Inspection Authority
   (Česká obchodní inspekce, https://www.coi.cz) as the body for
   out-of-court resolution of consumer disputes.

14. Governing law and disputes
   This Agreement is governed by the laws of the Czech Republic. The choice
   of law does not deprive a Consumer of the protection afforded by
   mandatory provisions of the law of the country of their habitual
   residence. Disputes are decided by the courts of the Czech Republic
   competent for the Licensor's registered office, unless the law provides
   otherwise for Consumers.

